PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
Most public responses favor ULDL (10/18): from @, go up through the top unlit hallway, left to the vertical passage, down to the gold-room row, then left through the door into the lit room containing the gold. This route avoids the red dragon entirely and is relatively direct. The main competing answer is DLDLUL (5/18), which goes down through the right-side lit room, left before the dragon, down to the lower door, left along the central unlit hallway, up, then left to gold. It also avoids stepping on the dragon, but it enters the dragon’s room and is longer, so it seems less safe unless lit areas are strongly preferred over unlit hallways. Outliers L, RULDL, and LULDL appear invalid or unjustified because they try to move immediately left/right from @ into non-corridor space or add unnecessary detours. Current best answer remains ULDL; key uncertainty is only whether unlit hallway exposure is considered a hazard, but ULDL still best avoids the known red dragon.
}

